# The desktop's screen mode and font, read by displayd when it starts (man zdesk "FILES"; man deskprefs).
# mode hires: 640 x 256 on a PAL Amiga, 640 x 200 on NTSC (steady on any monitor; 80 KB of chip RAM).
# mode hires-lace: interlaced, 640 x 512 PAL, 640 x 400 NTSC: twice the lines, the same 8-pixel font with twice the
#   rows; flickers on a TV or a 15 kHz monitor, steady through a flicker fixer or scandoubler; 160 KB of chip RAM
#   (hires when less than that and 512 KB more is free).
# mode auto (or no line): hires. PAL or NTSC is the machine's own, never set here.
# font NAME SIZE: the desktop's font (titles, the bar, menus, labels), an AmigaOS bitmap font copied as it is into
#   /usr/share/fonts/amiga (NAME.font and the NAME folder), e.g. "font helvetica 11"; a taller font makes the bar
#   and the title bars taller. font builtin (or no line): Topaz 8. Terminals always use the 8x8.
mode auto
